{
  "dom_id": "step-e15038",
  "name": "Example: Squaring Numbers Ending in Zeros",
  "problem": "Evaluate $220^2.$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate $220^2,$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131634/assets/9c2369ca7d3ec6a481dcbce12f4a9361daa241f44422cc04e74e3335bad6347e.svg)\n\nThen, we work out $220 \\times 220.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}220 & \\,⟶\\,220 \\\\ 220 & \\,⟶\\,220\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $2$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}484}{\\color{blue}00}= 48,400\n$$\n\nTherefore, $220^2  =   48,400.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
